<%- include('header'); -%>

<!-- Template for /help route -->

<p>
  This service allows to use external identities for <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Single_sign-on">single sign-on</a>.
</p>

<h3>Data being collected</h3>

<p>
  By using this service, you agree that the following data of authenticated identities is saved in our database and
  <strong>made available</strong> to selected applications:
</p>

<ul>
  <li>a freely chosen name for display (<tt>name</tt>)</li>
  <li>a unique and stable personal account identifier (<tt>uri</tt>)</li>
  <li>
    a list of <a href="./account">identities</a> connected to your account,
    each also with a name, identifier and additional data of the identity
  </li>
</ul>

<p>
  Applications may store and share the data by their own conditions.
  Passwords are <strong>never saved or shared in any way</strong>.
  This server also stores when the account was created and when it was used most
  lately, but these dates are not shared with applications.
</p>

<p>
  After logging in, you can see all data associated with your account at the
  <a href="./account">Account</a> page or by clicking on the <a href="currentUser">My Data</a> link
  in the footer. You will also be able to delete your user account which results in the immediate removal of all your data
  from our database. <b>Note</b> that data used in associated applications will <b>not</b> be deleted when deleting your user account.
</p>

<% if (config.applications.length) { %>
<h3>Applications</h3>
<p>
  The following applications are known to use <%= config.title %>:
  <ul>
    <% config.applications.forEach(application => { %>
    <li>
      <a href="<%= application.url %>" target="_blank">
        <%= application.name %>
      </a>
      <%= application.description %>
    </li>
    <% }) %>
  </ul>
  On the <a href="<%= baseUrl %>sessions">sessions page</a>, you can assess your currently active sessions and which applications have initiated them.
</p>
<% } %>

<%- include('footer'); -%>
